# Build context is the repository root so services can share vendor/wheels. Everything not needed
# to build an image is excluded — notably the secrets directory.
.secrets/
.env
.git/
*.docx
docs/
specs/
evidence/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/tests/
**/*.md

# ...except the Range's challenge content, which *is* the product. The rule above exists to keep
# documentation out of images; these files are data the service reads at runtime, and excluding them
# ships a Range with manifests and no material. The loud skip in content.py caught this once
# already, which is the only reason it is a comment rather than an outage.
!services/range/content/**/*.md
